    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d581">

                <pb facs="0852" n="738" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg738"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/1248: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Morgan</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-06-30T17:00:00-04:00">June 30, 1931—5
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>49. Your 42, June 29, 4 p.m. This Government and the neutral Governments are
                    counseling moderation on the part of both Bolivia and Paraguay and expressing
                    the hope that diplomatic relations will not be broken and that this incident
                    will be settled and will not be permitted to develop in such a way as to
                    endanger the holding of the conference suggested in the neutral Governments’
                    notes of June 25<anchor n="74" xml:id="d581-f1"/> for a settlement of the vital
                    Chaco question. Any support in this sense by the Brazilian Government will be
                    most welcome.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Castle</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
